Versus
The State represented by Sub-Inspector of Police, Oomachikulam Police Station, Madurai District
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Criminal Procedure 1973, Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita 2023, Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita 2023

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
CrPC Section 438, BNSS Section 482, BNS Section 115, BNS Section 352

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Anticipatory Bail, Pre-Arrest Bail, Civil Dispute, Custodial Interrogation, Cooperation

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Petitioner sought anticipatory bail in an FIR alleging boundary dispute altercation. No grievous injury was suffered by the complainant and weapon was already recovered.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether custodial interrogation is indispensable in land boundary scuffle when weapon is recovered?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Applying Arnesh Kumar and Satender Kumar Antil principles on personal liberty under Article 21 and Section 438 CrPC / 482 BNSS.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Where offense carries punishment under 7 years and custodial interrogation is unnecessary, anticipatory bail should normally be granted.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Anticipatory Bail Granted with conditions; Petitioner directed to appear before IO daily for 2 weeks.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice B. Pugalendhi
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
